      ":question/problem": "What is $\\sqrt[7]{2}$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The radical $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ can be written using a fractional exponent as ${x}^{1/n}.$\n\nComparing $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ with $\\sqrt[7]{2},$ we get $x=2,$ and $n=7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[7]{2}={2}^{1/7}\n$$",
